/*!
    \page target-page.html
    \title Target Page
    \brief A page to link to.

    This is the target page that we link to from the test page.
*/

/*!
    \page sa-multiline-link.html
    \title Multi-line See Also Links
    \brief Test that \\sa supports multi-line link syntax like \\l does.

    The purpose of this test is to verify that the \\sa command supports
    multi-line link syntax, where the link target and link text can be
    on different lines. This matches the documented behavior that \\sa
    supports the same kind of links as \\l.

    \section1 Test Cases

    This page tests multi-line \\sa syntax where {target} and {text}
    are on separate lines, which should work just like it does with \\l.

    \sa {target-page.html}
        {Link text on the next line}
*/

